dash='## Quant & Market Dashboard\n\n### Liquidity and volatility\n\n- **Weekend state:** U.S. cash equities are closed Sunday morning. Current ES/NQ depth, spreads, overnight volume, ETF executable quotes, Treasury liquidity and options positioning are unverified. Friday activity is a proxy only; refresh after futures reopen and before Monday’s cash auction.\n- **November 6 completed daily rows:** SPY 735.29, volume 58.98m; QQQ 656.10, volume 70.69m. Provider banners show different closing levels; reconcile against the execution feed rather than mixing snapshots. Volume does not measure depth. [SPY](https://chartexchange.com/symbol/nyse-spy/historical/) · [QQQ](https://chartexchange.com/symbol/nasdaq-qqq/historical/).\n- **Funding:** November 5 SOFR 3.92% versus EFFR 3.88%, a four-basis-point gap. Published November 6; lagged fixings do not establish current funding stress. [SOFR](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/SOFR) · [EFFR](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/EFFR).\n- **Regime: High; medium confidence.** November 6 delayed close VIX 25.64 at 4:00 p.m. EST / 3:00 p.m. CST, versus 28.18 November 5. House thresholds: below 15 low, 15–25 moderate, 25–35 high, above 35 stressed. This operating convention is not a calibrated forecast. Skew, term structure and dealer gamma remain unverified. [VIX](https://chartexchange.com/symbol/index-vix/historical/).\n\n### Factor proxies\n\n| Factor | ETF | Nov 5→6 | Oct 9→Nov 6 (4 weeks) |\n|---|---|---:|---:|\n'+rows+'\nPrice returns from the source-linked Close columns, excluding distributions; these are ETF proxies, not isolated factor premia. October 9 comparison inputs are archived from November 7; November 6 closes were rechecked today. Corporate-action histories were not independently refreshed; keep a common adjustment basis. Momentum and growth rebounded on Friday but remain sharply negative over four weeks; low volatility fell Friday but remains positive over that horizon.\n\n### Execution and microstructure\n\n- No regular SPY/QQQ trading session Sunday. For Monday November 9, cash opening auction is 8:30 a.m. CST / 14:30 UTC. Recheck the economic calendar before staging orders; CPI is Tuesday at 7:30 a.m. CST; check the full calendar before orders.\n- Inspect quote age, NBBO spreads, displayed depth, auction imbalances and ES/NQ basis. Use bounded limits and participation caps; stress gaps, cancellations, missed fills, latency and widened spreads. Rising prices on thin depth can trap liquidity takers.\n- Options: refresh post-expiry positions and hedge requirements; verify expiry, deliverables and settlement. Reject stale, crossed or one-sided quotes. Dealer-gamma sign, expiry concentrations and pinning remain unknown.\n\n**Research watchlist:** SPY, QQQ, IWM, RSP, TLT; ES, NQ, ZN, VX; MTUM, VLUE, QUAL, IWF, SPLV; BRK.B.\n\n### DRL Improvements for the MATLAB System\n\n1. Keep drawdown, exposure, participation and stale-data limits outside the policy, with a safe fallback.\n2. Penalize spread, impact, turnover, latency and missed fills; evaluate tail losses separately from reward.\n3. Keep future-return targets in training folds only; purge overlapping horizons and reserve a one-use final holdout.\n4. Randomize liquidity and observation delays across regimes; test whether abstention preserves risk compliance under distribution shift.\n\n### Model hygiene\n\nAudit leakage, survivorship bias, look-ahead, corporate actions, stale options quotes, multiple testing, calibration and drift. Use point-in-time universes, release vintages and availability timestamps. Fit preprocessing on training folds only; keep memory curation separate from point-in-time numerical evaluation.\n\n### MATLAB optimization patterns\n\n- Use named-zone timetables and causal synchronize/retime; never backfill unreleased observations.\n- Vectorize rolling features, preallocate logs and profile before optimizing.\n- Parallelize independent folds or Bayesian trials with reproducible random streams and fixed budgets.\n- Use GPUs for suitable batches; keep data, risk controls and evaluation in modular environments.\n\n### High-value quant research question\n\n**Does training-only forecast supervision improve net risk-adjusted results versus an identical policy without the auxiliary head?**\n\nMatch seeds, initial states, search budgets and costs; purge target horizons at fold boundaries. It tests whether forecast learning adds decision value without leakage.\n'
